<title>USA: Eastman to save $500 mln a year by YR 2000.</title>
<headline>Eastman to save $500 mln a year by YR 2000.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastman Chemical Co said Friday that it expects to cut $500 million a year in costs by the year 2000.</p>
<p>The company's senior vice president told analysts that the company should see $325 million in improvements in yearly labor costs and $175 million in yearly costs for materials, energy and supplies, according to a release. The savings should be achieved by the end of the decade, the company said.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to achieve the savings by improving productivity, outsourcing and investing in technology to cut labor costs.</p>
</text>
